{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Out in the west Texas town of El Paso
I fell in love with a Mexican girl.
Nighttime would fine me in Rosa's Cantina,
Music would play and Felina would whirl.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Black as the night were the eyes of Felina,
Wicked and evil while casting a spell.
My love was strong for this Mexican maiden,
I was in love, but in vain I could tell.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]One night a wild young cowboy came in, wild as the west Texas [D]wind...
[D]Dashing and daring, a drink he was sharing,
[D]With wicked Felina, the girl that I [G]love.
[A]So in anger
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I challenged his right for the love of this maiden;
Down went his hand for the gun that he wore.
My challenge was answered, in less than a heartbeat
The handsome young stranger lay dead on the floor.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Just for a moment I stood there in silence,
Shocked by the foul evil deed I had done.
Many thoughts ran through my mind as I stood there;
I had but one chance and that was to run.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Out through the back door of rose's I ran, out where the horses were tied
I picked a good one; he looked like he could run,
Up on his back and away I did ride.
Just as fast as
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
I could from the west Texas town of El Paso,
Out through the badlands of New Mexico.
Back in El Paso my life would be worthless;
Everything's gone in life nothing is left.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
But it's been so long since I've seen the young maiden,
My love is stronger that my fear of death.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 9}
I saddled up and away I did go, riding alone in the dark...
Maybe tomorrow a bullet may find me,
Tonight nothing's worse than this pain in my heart.
And as last here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 10}
I am on the hill overlooking El Paso,
I can see Rosa's Cantina below.
My love is strong and it pushes me onward,
down off the hill to Felina I go.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 11}
Off to my right I see five mounted cowboys,
Off to my left ride a dozen or more.
Shouting and shooting; I can't let them catch me,
I've got to make it to rose's back door.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 12}
Something is dreadfully wrong for I feel A deep burning pain in my side.
Though I am trying to stay in the saddle,
I'm getting weary, unable to ride.
But my love for
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 13}
Felina is strong and I rise where I've fallen.
Though I am weary, I can't stop to rest
I see the white puff of smoke from the rifle,
I feel the bullet go deep in my chest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 14}
From out of nowhere, Felina has found me,
Kissing my cheek as she kneels by my side.
Cradled by two loving arms that I'll die for,
One little kiss and Felina good-bye.
{end_of_verse}
